def test_sync_middleware_no_threadpool_deadlock_under_concurrency(): """Regression: a sync middleware that blocks on ``call_next`` plus a sync view must not exhaust anyio's shared threadpool under load.
Before the fix, the sync middleware borrowed a token from the shared limiter (40) and held it while blocking on the downstream sync view, which needed a second token — so >=40 concurrent requests deadlocked forever. """ api = _live_api() barrier = threading.Barrier(_PARKED, timeout=15)
